WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.202
-We did work together
down the hall earlier this year.

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:04.704
Because when I hosted "SNL," you
came back to play the President,

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:06.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is something you do.
-But isn't it weird how

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:09.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you're in and out of this
building for many years,

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:10.176 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it's like a blur.

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
You walk down the hall,
and you're like,

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:15.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Was that Belushi, Tom Brokaw,
you, Carson?"

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:18.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like one big ocean
of people that we've seen.

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:20.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And now you --
I guess the first time

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were in the building
was probably hosting?

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.657
I mean, I guess you'd maybe
been here for other things.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:27.093
-I did a soap opera here.
-You did a soap opera here?

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did a soap opera
on the third floor.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.163 line:92%
I did a soap opera here that --

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:31.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
which when I was on it,
I killed it.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
It went off the air
while I was on the show.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:34.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-I killed the show.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But does that mean
your character survived

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:38.138
if the show went off the air
before they could kill you?

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:40.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no. I'm saying
my acting killed the show.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, no,
but then, you know,

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:44.244
if you can get the show canceled
before they can

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:45.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
kill off your soap-opera
character,

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:48.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's a job well done.
-Yeah.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.082 line:92%
What I love about that show --

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's funny you say that.
This is true.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was killed by two people
simultaneously

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
unaware of
each other's presence.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:56.389 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh!

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.525
-One guy was aiming to shoot me
through the window

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:00.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
of an apartment
across the alleyway.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:03.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
And as he was aiming
to shoot me -- bing, bong.

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a knock at my door.
A guy I'm expecting.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.500
I open the door.
And he shoots me with a pistol.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the other guy
shoots me in the back.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
They both shot me
at the same time.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were
independent contractors.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, that's an impossible
murder to solve.

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I thought it was thrilling.
-Yeah.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.812
-It was amazing. Two guys
shot me at the same time,

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:19.979 line:92%
who were completely independent.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was obviously
an early job.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:22.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you upset
when that happened,

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:25.318
when you found out you'd been
killed off your soap-opera show?

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:29.122
-Whenever you're doing a job in
this business, when it's over,

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:31.591
you go through that thing like,
"Oh, I'll never work again."

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:34.828 size:84% position:42%
So, when the soap opera
was over, I was tense.

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought I'd never get
a job again.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then I went out to L.A.
and I did TV.

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:41.334 line:92%
-And then you hosted "SNL."

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.970
When you finished your first
time hosting, did you think,

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, I'm going to come back
and do this again?"

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:47.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No!
-Really?

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. No, no. That was 1990.
-Yeah.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:53.146
-And I didn't do "30 Rock"
or any kind of comedy stuff.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.581 line:92%
When I came on, I went home,

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I threw up all night
in my bathroom.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:00.019
"They're never going to ask me
to come back and do this again."

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:00.787 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-But, you know, you --

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.189
Obviously, as evidenced by how
many times they've had you back,

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.325
I think that's always
the most exciting kind of host,

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:08.228
is somebody who --
people don't know you did comedy

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:11.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
until you did that,
and then it was a revelation.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I think --
I say this all the time.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm not saying this
to be kind.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.771
But it's like, you know,
Tina, Carlock, you, Conan,

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:21.074
people like that,
they're funny 'cause they write.

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:22.041 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I don't write.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:24.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I'm just an actor.
And I say the lines.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
So when I would come on
and do the show,

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:27.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought this is the only,
you know --

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:31.217 size:84% position:42%
"SNL" was the only time
people would give me an
opportunity to do that.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:35.455
And eventually, in 2006,
we started doing "30 Rock."

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:39.192
But prior to that, this was
the only chance I could get to.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:42.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, plus, I was telling
Kevin backstage.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.097 line:92%
I was saying how, you know,

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:47.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
"SNL" is the only place
you could do certain things.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:48.635 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So, like, McKay --

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:50.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
Before Adam McKay became
a big, famous movie director,

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:52.805
he'd walk up to me and go,
"Okay, at the end of the sketch,

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're going to throw
the eggs at you.

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:55.208 line:92%
You're running for governor.

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.809
They're going to throw the eggs
at you. You're going turn.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
The eggs are going to hit you
in the backside.

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:00.480
And the woman is holding up
the baby for you to kiss.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.185
Then you grab the baby. And you
wipe your ass with the baby."

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:07.187 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:10.890
I remember sitting there going,
"Oh, my God."

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.558 size:75% position:38% line:92%
But then you realize

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:14.127
this is the only place in the
world that's going to happen.

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:18.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
It says "Governor Wheeler
wipes his ass with the baby."

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:22.702
-Yeah. And now that's not even
a big deal in politics. Yeah.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.103 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I want to -- I --

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I would like to say
that I wrote this sketch,

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:29.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the reality is David Mamet
wrote this sketch,

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:30.043 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and I just adapted it.

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:32.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this -- Every year
at Christmas, this ends up --

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:35.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is
"Glengarry Glen Christmas."

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.317 line:92%
And you sort of revisited --

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:38.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you wrote it.
-I did write it.

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:40.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, again, it was really
just David Mamet.

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:41.487 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Do you miss that?

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:44.691
On this show, how much writing
do you get to do on this show?

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:47.293
-Not as much.
-Not as much. Do you miss that?

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:48.461 line:92%
-I miss how thrilling it was

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:51.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
when something went
the way you wanted it to go,

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.832 line:92%
which doesn't happen that often.

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:55.401
-Did you write the Roger Stone?
Did you write the Roger Stone?

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:58.371
-I didn't write that joke,
but that was a great joke.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.672 line:92%
And it's also great to say them.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do like saying the jokes
my writers write me.

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:04.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was a -- You know,
especially at the table --

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now you know how I feel.
-Yeah.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:08.181
-I just say the jokes.
-Yeah, but you're a good actor.

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:10.083 line:92%
And I'm just a man at a desk.

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.251 line:92%
-That's why I waited five years.

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:12.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's why you waited
five years.

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:13.553 line:92%
-But when you wrote this --

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:16.723
People have asked me to do
this kind of thing before.

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:19.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
They've asked me
to do some Glengarry riff

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:20.793 line:92%
on this scene kind of thing.

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would never do it.
Never.

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:25.498
And you gave this -- I was like,
"God damn, it really is funny."

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:27.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So we did it. It was funny.

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:28.668 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I have one --

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:32.305
I have one prop from "SNL"
that I kept that's in my office.

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:34.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not actually
in this picture.

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:37.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a giant gumdrop
from that sketch.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:38.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:40.313 size:75% position:38%
-And when they said,
"Do you want this?"

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:41.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Yes."
And I brought it home.

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my wife said,
"Take it to the office."

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:47.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have one prop --
I have many other things.

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:51.090
But I have one prop from my desk
when I did "30 Rock."

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.358 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Which is I have a GE --

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:54.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
It said like,
"Global Business Leader."

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was glass little globe
of the Earth.

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:58.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just said,
"GE Global Business Leader."

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:01.100
And that's on my desk, too.
Now, is this a gift to me?

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.771
Are you giving this to me?
-You can take it if you want.

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:07.540 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

